--!strict
--[[
	Unlocks: the named milestones a business passes as its unit count grows.

	Copied from AdVenture Capitalist's Earth table. Each of the ten businesses has its own
	ladder, plus a "Capitalist" ladder gated on the *lowest* business -- you only earn those once
	every business has reached the mark.

	Two kinds, and the difference matters:

	* `speed` -- "Profit Speed Doubled", at 25/50/100/200/300/400. These are the cycle-time
	  halvings that `Economy.Cycle` already applies. They are listed here **for display only**;
	  applying them again would halve every cycle twice.
	* `profit` -- a straight profit multiplier. These start at 500 units and are genuinely new.
	  `target` is usually the owning business, "all" for the Capitalist ladder, or another
	  business entirely for Newspaper Delivery.

	Newspaper Delivery is the odd one out and the most interesting: from 125 units its unlocks
	are advertising deals that multiply *other* businesses' profits, on a 25-unit cadence. It
	turns an otherwise unremarkable business into the one you push for everyone else's sake.

	Carried to 1000 units per business. The source runs past 6000; this is already a long ladder
	and the pattern is plain for whoever extends it.

	Pure data. No logic, no functions, frozen.
]]

